Under the Public Health Service Act, 2075 (2018), the following rights are provided:

*   **Right to Quality Health Service:** Every citizen has the right to obtain quality health service in an easy and convenient manner [E2].
*   **Protection from Deprivation:** No citizen shall be deprived of health service [E2], [E3].
*   **Right to Free Basic Health Services:** Every citizen has the right to obtain free basic health services as prescribed, covering the following headings [E2], [E3]:
    *   Vaccination service [E2], [E3];
    *   Motherhood, infant, and pediatric health service (such as integrated infant and pediatric disease management, nutrition service, pregnancy, labor and childbirth service, family planning, abortion, and reproductive health) [E2], [E3];
    *   Service relating to communicable disease [E2], [E3];
    *   Service relating to non-communicable disease and physical disability [E2], [E3];
    *   Service relating to mental disease [E2], [E3];
    *   Service relating to elderly citizen's health [E2], [E3];
    *   Service of general emergency condition [E2], [E3];
    *   Ayurveda and other accredited alternative health service [E3]; and
    *   Other services prescribed by the Government of Nepal by notification in the Nepal Gazette [E3].

Additionally, the Act is enacted to implement the constitutionally guaranteed right to obtain free basic health service and emergency health service [E1].

